# Publish site updates to GitHub Pages

This website is a static site. GitHub Pages serves the `main` branch root of https://github.com/AAAA-web-deploy/JEPE.git

Live site: https://jensenpepe.xyz/

The custom domain is set by the `CNAME` file. Keep that file as `jensenpepe.xyz`. Public URLs in `index.html` (canonical, `og:url`, `og:image`, `twitter:image`) must use `https://jensenpepe.xyz/`.

When a requested change to this website is finished, commit it and push to `origin` `main`. GitHub Pages publishes the `main` branch root to https://jensenpepe.xyz/ on every push. After the push, confirm the new commit is the latest Pages build and that https://jensenpepe.xyz/ serves the update, then give that URL. A rebuild usually finishes within a couple of minutes.

- Do not force-push.
- Do not change git config.
- Do not commit secrets, tokens, or credential files.
- If the user is only asking a question, or explicitly says not to publish, do not commit or push.
